{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>He made me swear, saying.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded (Sotah 36b): and if you would say, let us release the oath — your oath too is subject to release. And according to the plain sense, the verse says <b>saying</b> because the oath was not in his own words as stated in Joseph's words to them, but rather it was the intent of the oath; therefore it says the word ״לֵאמֹר״ to say that the intent of what he said under oath was, etc.:" "<b>And by way of</b> derash it is possible that it intends to preclude Pharaoh's claim, for he might say to him: why did you not take counsel with him before the oath, and do a thing outside the king's knowledge? Therefore he said to him that he had no time to take counsel, because the declaration of the oath was close to his father's death, and this is what the verse says <b>He made me swear, saying, Behold I am dying</b> — meaning, at the time he made me swear he did not give me time, but rather said to me ״Behold I״ etc., and so it was, as I explained in the verse (Genesis 47:29) ״שִׂים נָא יָדְךָ״ etc., that he did not give him a long time, and truth did Joseph's mouth speak."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:51:17.440983685Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}